---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Anim from "../../components/Anim.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="@open-rgs/grid  - The board"
  description="Grid: Shape is a height PER COLUMN, not width x height."
>
  <main>
    <p class="dim"><a href="/extension">&larr; extensions</a></p>
    <h1>@open-rgs/grid</h1>

    <p class="lede">Shape is a height PER COLUMN, not width x height.</p>

    <Anim kind="grid" caption="The fifth cell exists in the tall reels and simply is not there in the short ones. Off-grid coordinates report rather than throw, because on a ragged board that is normal, not exceptional." />

    <p>Ragged reel sets are ordinary in production slots (4-5-5-5-5-4). An evaluator written against a rectangle bakes that assumption into every traversal, so adding ragged support later is not a feature - it is a rewrite of everything that reads a grid.</p>

    <h2 data-section="&sect;">Reach for</h2>
    <pre><code>{`import { ... } from "@open-rgs/grid";`}</code></pre>
    <p class="dim">rect(5, 3)  &middot;  makeGrid  &middot;  fromColumns  &middot;  at  &middot;  positionsWhere  &middot;  countOf  &middot;  withAt  &middot;  neighbours</p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
